data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":224,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_01cc20c3b29fc771016aca0f9301d48194afb5cabb6976b1c0","object":"response","created_at":1791627155,"completed_at":1791627182,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You are an expert coding assistant operating inside pi, a coding agent harness. You help users by reading files, executing commands, editing code, and writing new files.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nIn addition to the tools above, you may have access to other custom tools depending on the project.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for precise changes (edits[].oldText must match exactly)\n- When changing multiple separate locations in one file, use one edit call with multiple entries in edits[] instead of multiple edit calls\n- Each edits[].oldText is matched against the original file, not after earlier edits are applied. Do not emit overlapping or nested edits. Merge nearby changes into one edit.\n- Keep edits[].oldText as small as possible while still being unique in the file. Do not pad with large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about pi itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /usr/local/share/npm-global/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), pi packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- When working on pi topics, read the docs and examples, and follow .md cross-references before implementing\n- Always read pi .md files completely and follow links to related docs (e.g., tui.md for TUI API details)\n</docs>\n\n<addendum>\nKeep changes focused and readable. Use clear names and avoid needless duplication. Verify the changed behavior with appropriate checks before submitting.\n</addendum>\n\n<cwd>\n/home/agent/work\n</cwd>","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_01cc20c3b29fc771016aca0f947fa481949483bfd272aeeb73","summary":[{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Analyzing project snapshot issues**\n\nI'm trying to figure out the issue with the project page snapshots showing no summary and just a list of requirements. It seems like there's a checkbox for \"Complete Source\" that remains unchecked. The counts across checkboxes suggest that maybe the first checkbox needs to be checked off, but it’s not. There could be a mix-up with UI updates and an incorrect destination because of this reset. Also, the test on multiple destinations might not have been adequately verified."},{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Addressing DOM control issues**\n\nI need to ensure that the DOM controls for unchanged rows are retained to avoid race conditions while preserving destination data after any re-renders. It's critical that the checkbox event completes after modifications before the move occurs. There seems to be an issue with counting the rows, likely due to how source and transferred rows are managed. I could improve the system to robustly handle task states and ensure only the relevant rows are removed. I'll also look into how the ElementHandle locators are stored to make sure the move is successful."}],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABqyg-pLqRz7DdEFvt2_UtyBUw1oOnm9gNWBCwL3ToIuCMbpUv06jpDs1UwSH_lQ_u9Jk9dSOvWg9eVDO5UMndF7eqE6yQYo2J5AaU2zTy3PPWctGoV3TS-6WJr1m3O5x5J4yuCzYJWj9p-85C-52xVoDUrec6mIyL5iY4cAMr_BwPKybuMPaTPTGMDD0PoEpduNtzDbqS17CA048yj05Bf2TQ_9RrVhlL34pqrplSuUtGOEtsKBeYBm1lyQjJNBGul2iBKEilp2rbgOApbnIbQyoR3TiLKYaDwt0_p5mYn771_BP6-B3SeEFn7o7knkzYfpg-ErlkRi5YPLwUUP5JSo2YKfp9mk9zi_KOw8asyzcDyuXA2SuRhvZBGl1nDuWg0TBA201j5HPV4LVr98lBX3n9QQq_-9_2h7XRaOYN0AnuHZljR_ywzQSOjsXxjIzQMU9-J1FoQnLpcqaXks-3Wqc8TwXuhTozzuLjk2oZ0OoF8q79x7qJGv2olG-mPqoS-nHnBklPiaJZR6wyKqS2pwiKt3DcXfR46v6JFziFJdqXKtNT8bmx1I9aOoSXG3w8NFdEU3NpdMYDVP2VKDs10ZyvcShd7DBLknwbdzgamUgigGBg8wFnc6gdAyDuMnc7VeyeTrr4-iknGap47KuhvSUG5zi89nzMaHuFDLTWtbHIQ72Eo21sqeQPWbLX5bXhbxabJ1ZYoVvgXZa-A18Xfb3Sd4falWYzmZ-19HbOmYsTIaEe4Gb3-IkxQXGAiJ0iihLYgMZ-n142tFlEymV3PzaTqshOCnd7vBcsWXiIw2X_DEAnY3pIi7RY7WWEYeTGs0kMlxe5EueBTdOAeDMQCUBEmVHdyP4O0-7mOz_2LWkuUJ9JcIK2JHBVtd-ft4NORSB3-92aIeHnOrMmsjasv-bI562uKulxX6EPQpXU5ac8_i8MO7iBOnACul77F7CFnLwCQYQ8kiFCNwSafcmM_gv2knrUFuGPwDoB34qX46BNTSJ3wUH-Y0DbKOln3YxaJqU3ZcnPBz82pP574grlUW-ojg2Owi-ZLJOP0Kprz_k-rv9J-nNaaqZHTaGsSuPkqEF4oWBHuc833OZuCxmLAU1qNwohPkfoYRYYKXkU0BvmCSIP2NTA0EmOV2XG-SoaBtP2kR0ADz5-L8X3dhUbLE3pIIuq6owOM-1lzXdzaCrUCW0b6U5hX4_1CObBhbXxuRXgEaGduL1Sf_97qStBxtU_CTJNAg9jA-Fnj9MlbbfC_Er